  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India: the Handbook of Statistics on the Indian Economy, the RBI Bulletin, the Weekly Statistical Supplement and the Database on Indian Economy (DBIE), read from India Atlas's archived copy of these RBI publications. The printed tables' notes from the RBI Innovation Hub's copy of DBIE. GDP from MoSPI, read from this site's GDP guide; state GSDP ratios from the States guide. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={N["prov-vintage"]} />.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Amounts converted from rupees to ₹ crore; where a table prints one value per display unit, only actual values are read. Shares, ratios to revenue, ratios to GDP other than the RBI's, and shares of the budget estimate are India Atlas calculations, labelled as such. Every annual table is checked against the printed Handbook and every identity the tables state is tested. Nothing is estimated.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Accounts, revised estimates and budget estimates are separate series. Ratios to GDP are kept apart by GDP base. Other breaks kept apart: small savings receipts (gross to March 2017, net after); 'others' among bondholders (pension funds separate from March 2022); two layouts of the ownership table; the Bulletin's monthly accounts, whose old layout counts borrowing inside receipts.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026. Revised with each month's Union accounts and each annual Handbook.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <span>India Atlas, government budgets and debt</span>
      <span>Vintage <span id="prov-vintage2" set:html={N["prov-vintage2"]} /></span>
      <span>Set in Source Serif 4 and Golos Text</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

